  "title": "DCT2000: Allow any PDU to be dissected if it lacks lower layers.",
  "description": "There are traffic dumps that only include the PDU payload\nwithout lower layer information.  This commit allows any\ndissector to be embedded in the DCT2000 as a protocol name.\ntshark/wireshark will decode it despite having no lower\nlayer information.\n\nThe change allows the specified DCT2000 protocol to be used\nto look for a dissector.\n\nExample:\n\n```\nSession Transcript (format 3.1)\nDecember 6, 2020     16:45:20.5185\nLTE-RRC.1/lte_rrc.dl_dcch/1/// r tm 22.5695 l $2c02\nS1AP.1/s1ap/1/// s tm 23.3926 l $001700130000020063000608023d7c00830002400202a0\n```",
  "state": "closed",
